From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:50:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 444/488] [DS4.1] Disk Engram columns all-gathered with no
 copies

A rank's row gather writes its own hash columns side by side, and the
all-gather takes them as 256-wide rows along the last dimension: rank
r's k-th block lands at column k * tp + r, the column order, so neither
the strided slice before the collective nor the transpose after it
remains.
